"},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 12.6% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $393.5m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1788882/000178888226000047/0001788882-26-000047-index.htm","accession":"0001788882-26-000047"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in all 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1788882/000178888226000047/0001788882-26-000047-index.htm","accession":"0001788882-26-000047"},{"text":"Net cash of $396.9m against total assets of $1.7bn - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1788882/000178888226000047/0001788882-26-000047-index.htm","accession":"0001788882-26-000047"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (0.0% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1788882/000178888226000047/0001788882-26-000047-index.htm","accession":"0001788882-26-000047"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 105.1% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1788882/000178888226000047/0001788882-26-000047-index.htm","accession":"0001788882-26-000047"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 1.3% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1788882/000162828026044895/0001628280-26-044895-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metr